        "note_type": "progress note",
        "text": "85-year-old male presents with progressive blurred vision and glare OD over the past 12 months, significantly impacting driving and reading. BCVA OD 20/70, not improving with refraction. Slit lamp reveals 3+ nuclear sclerosis with PSC. Glare testing shows marked reduction in contrast sensitivity. B-scan confirms normal posterior segment. Patient desires surgical correction. Plan: phacoemulsification with PCIOL OD. Discussed risks including endophthalmitis, retinal detachment, PCR, and need for postop drops. Patient consents. Requesting PA for CPT 66984."
